snp3.12:25.1 starts: “Knowing that
snp3.12:25.2 starts: pleasure, pain,
snp3.12:25.3 starts: neither pleasure nor pain,
snp3.12:25.4 starts: within or without—
snp3.12:26.1 starts: is stressful;
snp3.12:26.2 starts: seeing
snp3.12:26.3 starts: its passing away
snp3.12:26.4 starts: he knows it right there:
snp3.12:26.5 starts: With just the ending of feeling,
snp3.12:26.6 starts: there is no stress
snp3.12:36.1 starts: his craving for becoming crushed,
snp3.12:36.2 starts: his mind at peace,
snp3.12:36.3 starts: his wandering-on in birth totally ended:
snp3.12:36.4 starts: He has no further becoming.
snp3.12:57.1 starts: The stopping of self-identity
snp3.12:57.2 starts: is viewed by the noble ones
snp3.12:57.3 starts: This, when seen,
snp3.12:57.4 starts: to the whole world.
snp4.1:3.1 starts: Whoever avoids sensual desires
snp4.1:3.2 starts: —as he would, with his foot,
snp4.1:3.3 starts: goes beyond, mindful,
snp4.1:3.4 starts: this attachment in the world.
snp4.1:4.1 starts: A man who is greedy
snp4.1:4.2 starts: for fields, land, gold,
snp4.1:4.3 starts: servants, employees,
snp4.1:4.4 starts: many sensual pleasures,
